sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor S as Student
  participant UI as StudyBuddyApp (UI)
  participant CC as ChatCore
  participant SF as Safety
  participant IR as IntentRouter and direct handlers
  participant TO as ToolOrchestrator
  participant PB as Prompt builder
  participant LL as Ollama llama3.2:3b
  participant DB as memory.db
  participant EX as Extractor (rules)
  participant PC as PersonalCompanion

  S->>UI: types a message
  UI->>CC: handle_message(text)
  CC->>SF: check_language
  alt not English
    SF-->>UI: fixed English-only reply (not saved)
    UI-->>S: shows reply
  else English
    CC->>SF: check_input (none, medium or high)
    alt high risk
      CC->>DB: save turn with fixed safety reply
      CC-->>UI: fixed safety reply (no model call)
      UI-->>S: shows reply
    else none or medium
      CC->>IR: try code-only paths first
      Note over CC,IR: In order: busy reply to a nudge, My World check-in, pending dialog, nudge feedback, memory transparency, desktop context, name questions, greeting, capability and memory access, intent confirmation, task, reminder and timer commands
      alt handled by code
        IR-->>CC: result without a model call
        CC->>DB: run approved handler, save turn
        CC-->>UI: reply
        UI-->>S: shows reply
      else needs the model
        CC->>TO: tools_for_text (BM25, embedding fallback only if weak)
        TO-->>CC: 0 to 4 tool names
        CC->>PB: safety core, persona, confirmed memory, profile card, camera text if camera is on
        Note over CC,PB: Medium risk skips persona and profile card and adds extra-care text
        PB-->>CC: system prompt and recent turns
        opt tools were selected
          CC->>TO: run(messages)
          TO->>LL: request with tool schemas
          LL-->>TO: tool call
          TO->>DB: run allow-listed handler (arguments validated)
        end
        CC->>LL: chat (or final pass after the tool result)
        LL-->>CC: streamed reply
        CC->>SF: safe_output (also checked while streaming)
        CC->>CC: fix wrong name claim, prepend fixed care opening if medium
        CC->>DB: save turn
        opt risk is none and tier_facts is on
          CC->>EX: extract candidates (regex, no model call)
          EX-->>CC: up to 3 candidates
          CC->>PC: add candidate to queue
          PC->>DB: personal_nodes and candidate_queue
          Note over CC,PC: Candidates stay out of prompts until confirmed (stored as confirmed if the student opted into My World memory)
        end
        CC-->>UI: reply
        UI-->>S: shows reply
      end
    end
  end
